;; IPv4/IPv6 with DHCP on the primary interface.

;; Note what this does NOT state: which DHCP client to use.
;;
;; It named BR2_PACKAGE_DHCPCD until two images proved that wrong. Under
;; profile:minimal, BusyBox udhcpc and dhcpcd both ran and both took the same
;; lease. Under profile:standard, systemd-networkd won the race and dhcpcd
;; failed at every boot. The feature was asserting a mechanism where it wanted an
;; outcome, and each profile already supplies its own.
(fragment feature:networking

  (requires
    (capability dhcp-client))

  (buildroot
    (value BR2_SYSTEM_DHCP "eth0"))

  (linux
    (y CONFIG_INET)
    ;; dhcpcd needs AF_PACKET to do raw DHCP. Nothing in the Linux tree knows that,
    ;; and nothing in the Buildroot tree can say it — cross-tree, therefore stated.
    (y CONFIG_PACKET)
    (prefer y CONFIG_IPV6)))

;; Derived, therefore absent: CONFIG_NET (depended on by INET).
